From: ProjectM TV contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Avoid PowerVR framebuffer blits with a cached textured copy

The reporter's released 2.3.55 ARM backtrace enters the PowerVR driver at
 glBlitFramebuffer from Renderer::Framebuffer::SetSize. The rebuild has identical
.text bytes/addresses to that released library, identifying the resize copy.
Use the existing Shader and Sampler implementations for a cached fullscreen draw
on PowerVR, including resize, detail recombination and host-scaled presentation.
Resize all attachments before preserving colour zero and restrict colour copies
to that target so auxiliary/integer attachments cannot receive normalized data.
Other GPUs retain framebuffer blits. Pixel/state and no-blit controls cover the
compatibility path; affected-device confirmation is still required.

---
